    "",
    "Checksums are NOT listed here. Neither project publishes .sha256 files, but GitHub exposes",
    "a sha256 digest for every release asset through its API, and the installer reads it there.",
    "Pinning a hash in this file stays possible (asset.sha256) and takes precedence — use it only",
    "when a specific file must be guaranteed, because a pinned hash goes stale on every version",
    "bump and a stale hash blocks installs for everyone.",
    "",
    "Bumping a loader version = change 'version', the release 'tag', and the asset names.",
    "",
        "Each warning carries the situation it applies to (os / runtimes / on_fresh_install). A note",
    "shown when it is not true teaches the reader to skip warnings, which is the one habit they",
    "must not have. Facts about platforms we do not offer belong in this comment, not on screen."
